1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,692
Most trading demos begin with a chart going up and to the right.

2
00:00:04,692 --> 00:00:09,024
Finly asks what survives before that chart gets anywhere near a broker.

3
00:00:09,444 --> 00:00:16,764
We replaced the frozen SPY and BIL policy's same-close assumption with next-session-open fills.

4
00:00:16,764 --> 00:00:19,016
Across 415 consumed sessions,

5
00:00:19,016 --> 00:00:22,958
after five basis points per traded-notional leg,

6
00:00:22,958 --> 00:00:28,589
it returned 15.39 percent with a 5.45 percent maximum drawdown.

7
00:00:28,589 --> 00:00:33,656
At 25 basis points, it still returned 10.56 percent.

8
00:00:33,656 --> 00:00:38,724
SPY returned 33.52 percent. Finly did not beat it.

9
00:00:39,144 --> 00:00:45,953
At one basis point per traded leg, a $300 shadow ended at $351.88.

10
00:00:45,953 --> 00:00:49,619
The preview enforced a $1 order minimum,

11
00:00:49,619 --> 00:00:51,714
skipped twelve sub-dollar adjustments,

12
00:00:51,714 --> 00:00:53,809
used nine-decimal fractional sizing,

13
00:00:53,809 --> 00:00:56,951
and charged a $0.70 sell-fee proxy.

14
00:00:56,951 --> 00:01:02,712
That tests affordability and mechanics. It is not a broker fill.

15
00:01:03,132 --> 00:01:05,678
The policy is deliberately boring.

16
00:01:05,678 --> 00:01:10,262
Three lagged SPY minus BIL trend horizons set exposure,

17
00:01:10,262 --> 00:01:15,864
a ten-percent volatility target scales it, and BIL receives the rest.

18
00:01:15,864 --> 00:01:20,956
AI may interpret evidence and veto. Deterministic code owns exposure,

19
00:01:20,956 --> 00:01:24,012
order fields, maximum loss, and permission.

20
00:01:24,432 --> 00:01:31,632
The supportive synthetic fixture survived four of four source removals and thirty-two of thirty-two perturbations.

21
00:01:31,632 --> 00:01:36,432
In the conflicting fixture, removing one source changed the decision,

22
00:01:36,432 --> 00:01:38,832
so Finly returned no trade.

23
00:01:38,832 --> 00:01:43,152
A surviving fixture can compile a defined-risk SPY spread,

24
00:01:43,152 --> 00:01:47,472
here with $366 maximum loss and $634 maximum gain,

25
00:01:47,472 --> 00:01:48,912
without transmitting it.

26
00:01:49,332 --> 00:01:54,610
Even the strongest backtest did not receive authority.

27
00:01:54,610 --> 00:02:01,867
G4 turned a modeled $100,000 into $1,067,106, versus $680,817 for SPY.

28
00:02:01,867 --> 00:02:09,124
But it was selected after history was viewed and failed multiple-testing,

29
00:02:09,124 --> 00:02:14,402
growth-control, and source-overlap gates. Finly kept the chart,

30
00:02:14,402 --> 00:02:19,020
labeled it consumed, and rejected the strategy.

31
00:02:19,440 --> 00:02:22,416
Attempt 114 answers that hindsight problem.

32
00:02:22,416 --> 00:02:24,896
Before the first eligible signal,

33
00:02:24,896 --> 00:02:32,336
a public GitHub workflow verified 17 bound runtime files through 23 fixed public GET checks.

34
00:02:32,336 --> 00:02:38,288
The protocol requires 254 consecutive timely commitment anchors and 252 reconciled settlements,

35
00:02:38,288 --> 00:02:41,760
with no skipped sessions, backfill, replacement windows,

36
00:02:41,760 --> 00:02:44,736
optional stopping, or second confirmatory try.

37
00:02:45,156 --> 00:02:49,392
That record is not an independent cryptographic timestamp,

38
00:02:49,392 --> 00:02:53,099
provider-origin proof, broker fill, or profitability result.

39
00:02:53,099 --> 00:02:59,454
Today there is no prospective performance inference and no broker mutation authority.

40
00:02:59,454 --> 00:03:01,572
Alpaca access remains read-only.

41
00:03:01,992 --> 00:03:06,103
Finly is not a bigger forecast. It is a smaller,

42
00:03:06,103 --> 00:03:09,802
testable trust boundary: let AI interpret more, authorize less,

43
00:03:09,802 --> 00:03:13,091
and make correction, rejection, and no trade visible.

44
00:03:13,091 --> 00:03:18,024
The bull has horns. The llama still does not get the keys.
